# One line ending everywhere: LF in the repository, LF in the working tree, LF in
# `git archive` output (the tree is shipped to a mac via git archive | tar, and a stray CRLF
# breaks a shebang). Git enforces it, so nobody has to remember it.
#
# The eye this mirror syncs from is LF by the same rule; scripts/sync_from_eye.sh also converts
# every text file it writes, so a CRLF working copy on the Windows side cannot leak in.
# No file here needs CRLF (no .bat/.cmd/.ps1; no test reads raw \r\n bytes from a file).
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary types present in the tree (by type, not by guess).
*.png binary

# Historical one-off debug scripts stay in git but out of deploys.
scripts/debug/ export-ignore
